<<<cmd
# tree-sitter corpus "Extra complex literals in expressions": this input is
# DELIBERATELY MALFORMED JS (`if ({a:'b'} {c:'d'})` — two adjacent objects, no
# operator). tree-sitter's own expected output contains (ERROR ...) and
# (MISSING ";"): it error-RECOVERS into a tree. tinyparse instead flags the
# syntax error and rejects (exit non-zero). Both detect the error; matching
# tree-sitter's exact error-recovery tree is separate future work, not JS
# language coverage. All 115 VALID corpus cases parse cleanly.
"$TP" run std.javascript --input test/suite/jsfamily/inputs/destructuring__5.js --dump-tree
